    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Part 1: R_V Fundamentals (Synthetic Data)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Understanding the Participation Ratio\n",
    "\n",
    "The **participation ratio (PR)** measures effective dimensionality:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$PR = \\frac{(\\sum_i \\sigma_i^2)^2}{\\sum_i \\sigma_i^4}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where $\\sigma_i$ are singular values of the activation matrix.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **High PR**: Information distributed across many dimensions\n",
    "- **Low PR**: Information concentrated in few dimensions (geometric contraction)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstrate PR computation with synthetic data\n",
    "\n",
    "def create_baseline_activation(seq_len=64, dim=512, n_dominant=50):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Create synthetic 'baseline' activation with distributed information.\n",
    "    Simulates standard processing where information spreads across dimensions.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Many directions with moderate singular values\n",
    "    U = np.random.randn(seq_len, dim)\n",
    "    s = np.exp(-np.linspace(0, 2, min(seq_len, dim)))  # Gradual decay\n",
    "    s[:n_dominant] *= 2  # Some structure but still distributed\n",
    "    Vt = np.random.randn(min(seq_len, dim), dim)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Construct activation matrix\n",
    "    activation = U[:, :len(s)] @ np.diag(s) @ Vt\n",
    "    return activation, s\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def create_recursive_activation(seq_len=64, dim=512, n_dominant=15):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Create synthetic 'recursive' activation with concentrated information.\n",
    "    Simulates self-referential processing with geometric contraction.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Few directions with large singular values (concentrated)\n",
    "    U = np.random.randn(seq_len, n_dominant)\n",
    "    U, _ = np.linalg.qr(U)  # Orthonormal\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Strong concentration in few dimensions\n",
    "    s = np.array([10.0 / (k+1) for k in range(n_dominant)])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Project to full dimensionality\n",
    "    V = np.random.randn(dim, n_dominant)\n",
    "    V, _ = np.linalg.qr(V)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    activation = U @ np.diag(s) @ V.T\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Add small noise\n",
    "    activation += 0.1 * np.random.randn(seq_len, dim)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return activation, s\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate sample activations\n",
    "baseline_act, baseline_s = create_baseline_activation()\n",
    "recursive_act, recursive_s = create_recursive_activation()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute PR for both\n",
    "baseline_pr = compute_participation_ratio(baseline_s)\n",
    "recursive_pr = compute_participation_ratio(recursive_s)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Singular Value Decay:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Baseline:   {baseline_s[:5].round(2)}... (PR={baseline_pr:.1f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Recursive:  {recursive_s[:5].round(2)}... (PR={recursive_pr:.1f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nContraction ratio: {recursive_pr/baseline_pr:.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
